Z||000004||artherd||12-31-2001||08:23 PM||||Hi Jim, oh, awesome!!<P>Thanks buddy, no hurry (I don't even have the intake parts to attach them to yet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Enjoy the season! HAPPY NEW YEAR!!!<P>PS:  see? told you Jim rocks.<P>PPS: Speedflow has 100% TEFLON hose up to I belive -6AN and hose ends with Power Steering  type connectors, might be a good idea with upur pump in back and the rack upfront?<P>You need the TEFLON 200 series hose, because of extreemly high hydraulic pressures involved. (up to 2-3,000psi, similar to hydraulic brake systems. Infact, the 200series hoses is basically for brake lines.)<P>Just look on their website, then feed Jim some part numbers! (after a few days  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B> Will have those other prices to you soon ben. I am trying to have a little holiday for a few days.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
